From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:32:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ui/egl-helpers: import dma-bufs with
 glEGLImageTargetTexStorageEXT

egl_dmabuf_import_texture() binds an imported dma-buf EGLImage with

    glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES(GL_TEXTURE_2D, image);

NVIDIA hands out the guest's scanout buffers as *external-only*
EGLImages and rejects that call: measured on an RTX 4070 with driver
595.84, the 2D bind returns GL_INVALID_OPERATION (0x0502) while
glEGLImageTargetTexStorageEXT (GL_EXT_EGL_image_storage) succeeds on
the very same image.  The failure is silent from the user's side --
QEMU imports every frame, drops it, and shows a black window under
-display gtk,gl=on.

Without this the only working present path is
NVKVM_PRESENT_MODE=readback, which costs a full ~8 MB glReadPixels per
frame on the main loop and cannot hold 60fps at 1080p.  So this patch
is what makes the zero-copy present path usable at all, not a
micro-optimisation.

The lookup is done once through eglGetProcAddress and cached in a
function-local static, and falls back to the original OES bind when the
extension is absent, so a driver that does not have
EXT_EGL_image_storage behaves exactly as before.

This is the same fix as nvkvm_import_dmabuf_tex() in
src/qemu/nvkvm_present_egl.c -- nvkvm's own present path already does
it; this patch teaches QEMU's shared helper the same thing, because the
gtk/egl-headless display paths go through the helper and not through
ours.

Not obviously upstreamable as written: upstream would want an explicit
EXT_EGL_image_storage capability check rather than "did the symbol
resolve", and would want it tested against Mesa as well as NVIDIA.
Keep it downstream until someone does that work.
---
 ui/egl-helpers.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/egl-helpers.c b/ui/egl-helpers.c
index 81a57fa..b2d69ed 100644
--- a/ui/egl-helpers.c
+++ b/ui/egl-helpers.c
@@ -354,7 +354,23 @@ void egl_dmabuf_import_texture(QemuDmaBuf *dmabuf)
     glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
     glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
 
-    glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES(GL_TEXTURE_2D, (GLeglImageOES)image);
+    {
+        /* nvkvm: NVIDIA rejects the legacy OES bind for external-only
+         * dma-buf images (GL_INVALID_OPERATION); EXT_EGL_image_storage
+         * takes the same image as immutable GL_TEXTURE_2D storage. */
+        static PFNGLEGLIMAGETARGETTEXSTORAGEEXTPROC nvkvm_tex_storage;
+        static bool nvkvm_looked_up;
+        if (!nvkvm_looked_up) {
+            nvkvm_looked_up = true;
+            nvkvm_tex_storage = (PFNGLEGLIMAGETARGETTEXSTORAGEEXTPROC)
+                eglGetProcAddress("glEGLImageTargetTexStorageEXT");
+        }
+        if (nvkvm_tex_storage) {
+            nvkvm_tex_storage(GL_TEXTURE_2D, (GLeglImageOES)image, NULL);
+        } else {
+            glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES(GL_TEXTURE_2D, (GLeglImageOES)image);
+        }
+    }
     eglDestroyImageKHR(qemu_egl_display, image);
 }
 
